1
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:09,440
YAMU! YAMU!

2
00:00:09,940 --> 00:00:12,337
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

3
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:13,300
YAMU!

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,540
Your moves!

5
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,320
It's time to duel!

6
00:01:02,120 --> 00:01:04,532
Looks like you're defenseless now, Kaiba.

7
00:01:05,860 --> 00:01:06,960
That's the brakes.

8
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:09,777
And you said I didn't
belong in your tournament.

9
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:11,213
Care to take that back?

10
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:13,680
Yeah, you tell him, Joey.

11
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:16,540
He just might beat that
rich snob after all.

12
00:01:17,260 --> 00:01:19,320
Joey's doing awesome against Kaiba.

13
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:24,144
He's become one of the
greatest duelists around.

14
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:30,247
He could have won this whole tournament
if it wasn't for Merrick's Shadow Game.

15
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:34,120
Winged Dragon of Ra, brain his soul.

16
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:38,940
The shadows await.

17
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:44,500
You're standing, but how?

18
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:51,497
If he succeeds in
attacking my life points,

19
00:01:51,580 --> 00:01:55,080
I'll lose the duel and
my intimation god card.

20
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:57,700
All right, this is it.

21
00:01:57,960 --> 00:01:59,620
Here goes nothing.

22
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:05,740
This guy can wipe Marek out.

23
00:02:06,880 --> 00:02:10,700
Now, I summon Garefreed the Iron Knight!

24
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:12,750
No!

25
00:02:13,060 --> 00:02:14,600
This can't be possible!

26
00:02:14,940 --> 00:02:17,058
Hurry up and call your attack, Joey!

27
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:19,790
I...

28
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:23,810
Joey!

29
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:25,600
Get up, man!

30
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:26,800
Get up!

31
00:02:28,060 --> 00:02:32,001
All he had to do was yell attack,
and Joey would have won the duel.

32
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:34,050
Hmm.

33
00:02:34,133 --> 00:02:34,963
But in his heart,

34
00:02:35,046 --> 00:02:38,679
Joey knows that he's a great duelist
worthy of the Battle City crowd.

35
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:41,857
Joey's dueling pretty well against Seto,

36
00:02:41,940 --> 00:02:44,881
but he'll have to do better
than that to beat him.

37
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:48,800
Well, congratulations
on making one good move.

38
00:02:49,020 --> 00:02:51,177
There is a first time for everything.

39
00:02:51,260 --> 00:02:52,090
Watch it, pal.

40
00:02:52,173 --> 00:02:54,400
I'm not your pal, Wheeler.

41
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:55,560
If I were,

42
00:02:55,780 --> 00:02:58,197
I'd be standing over there
with the other geeks cheering

43
00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:01,574
my pathetic heart out for the
obvious loser of the duel.

44
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:05,557
Did you forget that I destroyed
every powerful monster in your deck?

45
00:03:05,640 --> 00:03:06,470
He's right.

46
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:08,057
Thanks to his crush card,

47
00:03:08,140 --> 00:03:11,837
the only monsters I got left have
less than 1,500 attack points.

48
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:13,449
But I gotta keep fighting.

49
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:17,017
If I let Kaivah get the best of me,
he'll never let me live it down.

50
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:19,394
And I gotta put that punk in his place.

51
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:20,977
You can do this, Joey.

52
00:03:21,060 --> 00:03:23,420
Thanks, Yug. I needed that.

53
00:03:23,980 --> 00:03:24,810
Ha!

54
00:03:24,893 --> 00:03:26,360
You don't have a clue, do you?

55
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:27,520
Now let's duel!

56
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:32,257
It's time I gave you a first-hand look
at the difference in our skill levels!

57
00:03:32,340 --> 00:03:33,693
So stand back, Wheeler!

58
00:03:33,900 --> 00:03:37,200
I play Blade Knight in attack mode!

59
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:40,780
Now attack his swordsman!

60
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:48,710
Whoa!

61
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:49,750
That's rough!

62
00:03:49,833 --> 00:03:53,057
He just lost half his life
points one more attack

63
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:56,580
like that Joey's done
he'll pull through well,

64
00:03:56,760 --> 00:03:58,020
let's just hope so

65
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:06,460
Now I shall place one card
face down you have no chance.

66
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:08,140
I'm just getting warmed up

67
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:10,100
So watch out

68
00:04:15,540 --> 00:04:18,920
I must discover what
happened up here today

69
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:23,540
When the two Egyptian gods
clashed, something was released.

70
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:36,180
The force created by these two behemoths
caused my Millennium Rod to activate.

71
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:41,120
According to the Pharaoh, he and
Kaiba were shown a vision of the past.

72
00:04:41,860 --> 00:04:43,700
But what did they see?

73
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:47,720
And why is my Millennium
Item serving anyone but me?

74
00:04:48,620 --> 00:04:51,032
Only I should control the Millennium Rod.

75
00:04:51,900 --> 00:04:55,320
I command you to obey me now! Hear me?

76
00:04:55,680 --> 00:04:59,920
Show me the ancient images that
you showed the Pharaoh and Kaiba!

77
00:05:07,760 --> 00:05:09,936
You should be more careful with this.

78
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:13,400
Pardon me?

79
00:05:16,380 --> 00:05:18,900
My move, rich boy. Here it goes.

80
00:05:19,960 --> 00:05:21,607
What do you say we try this?

81
00:05:22,340 --> 00:05:23,300
Check it out.

82
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:25,880
I summon little Wingard in attack mode.

83
00:05:28,760 --> 00:05:29,960
What's up with that?

84
00:05:30,340 --> 00:05:34,677
Joey's monster is weaker than Kaiba's,
but he played it in attack mode, dude.

85
00:05:34,760 --> 00:05:38,760
Yeah, he just broke the most basic
rule of winning at duel monsters.

86
00:05:38,900 --> 00:05:40,457
What are you thinking, Wheeler?

87
00:05:40,540 --> 00:05:43,420
Is this some lame attempt at a strategy?

88
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:44,830
Maybe.

89
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:46,957
Why don't you judge for yourself?

90
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:49,620
I play the magic card, Legendary Sword.

91
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:54,118
The monster that holds this sword
gains 300 attack and defense points.

92
00:05:54,700 --> 00:05:55,640
Great move.

93
00:05:55,980 --> 00:06:00,140
Now you can strengthen your Wingard
and take down Kaiba's Knight.

94
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:03,125
Now, little Wingard, draw
your Legendary Sword.

95
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:06,460
Well, I activate this...

96
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:09,057
Absorb spell. Oh, boy.

97
00:06:09,140 --> 00:06:12,057
Now the magic card you
just combined with your

98
00:06:12,140 --> 00:06:15,000
wing guard is transferred
to my blade knight,

99
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:17,182
making my monster even stronger.

100
00:06:19,580 --> 00:06:21,820
You stole my legendary sword.

101
00:06:22,620 --> 00:06:24,380
And my attack points.

102
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:28,188
That was a third-rate strategy,
Wheeler, just as I suspected.

103
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:31,660
You could never defeat a
duelist with real talent.

104
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:35,737
Well, next time I'm dueling someone
with talent, I'll remember that.

105
00:06:35,820 --> 00:06:38,140
Now I'll place one card face down.

106
00:06:39,140 --> 00:06:40,260
Your move, Kaiba.

107
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:43,920
I hate to admit it, but
Kaiba's a tough customer. Yeah?

108
00:06:44,340 --> 00:06:45,860
Well, Joey is, too.

109
00:06:46,300 --> 00:06:48,540
Take a good look at his eyes, Duke.

110
00:06:48,860 --> 00:06:51,900
Joey is determined to win
this duel no matter what.

111
00:06:54,020 --> 00:06:55,700
Hand over that item.

112
00:06:56,360 --> 00:07:01,300
You are meddling with forces
beyond your control. Return it.

113
00:07:08,140 --> 00:07:12,980
what's going on no one can
use the millennium rod but me

114
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:20,257
what's the deal with the
puzzle it's glowing i have a

115
00:07:20,340 --> 00:07:23,693
strange feeling that whatever's
causing this is not good.

116
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:26,990
Taya!

117
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:31,997
Something's wrong with Taya.

118
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:34,100
We've got to go find her. Now!

119
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:39,100
I'll be right back, Joey. Stay strong.

120
00:07:42,540 --> 00:07:45,952
You may think I'm going to
attack your pitiful wing guard.

121
00:07:47,380 --> 00:07:50,197
But I've got other things
planned for you, Wheeler.

122
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:54,456
and I'm afraid they're much worse
than anything you could ever imagine.

123
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:57,480
Watch and learn, you amateur.

124
00:07:58,720 --> 00:08:02,220
I activate the magic
card enemy controller.

125
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:05,060
Here's how it works.

126
00:08:05,700 --> 00:08:10,900
I drop a thousand life points to
take control of one of your monsters.

127
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:15,100
Left, right, A, B.

128
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:17,040
And now it's showtime.

129
00:08:17,440 --> 00:08:19,860
Your puny warrior is mine.

130
00:08:21,220 --> 00:08:22,900
You're wide open, Wheeler.

131
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:25,540
Now to play one of my magic cards.

132
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:27,960
It's called Cough Down,

133
00:08:28,220 --> 00:08:32,573
and it lowers the level of one of my
monsters, making it easier to summon.

134
00:08:32,980 --> 00:08:34,000
No way!

135
00:08:34,260 --> 00:08:36,997
Now I shall summon a monster
that usually requires

136
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:40,400
two sacrifices by
sacrificing only one card.

137
00:08:41,420 --> 00:08:42,480
All right.

138
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:45,400
Prepare to meet my ultimate beast.

139
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:48,080
I sacrifice your little wing guard.

140
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:54,140
In order to summon this card,
my Blue-Eyes White Dragon.

141
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:02,540
How can I protect myself from that?

142
00:09:04,700 --> 00:09:06,780
Now you're defenseless.

143
00:09:07,340 --> 00:09:11,260
So one attack by my Blue-Eyes
and you lose the duel.

144
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:14,287
You should have quit
when you had the chance.

145
00:09:14,380 --> 00:09:18,760
Blue-Eyes White Dragon, attack
his life points directly!

146
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:22,120
Do something and do it fast!

147
00:09:23,460 --> 00:09:25,040
Hold on, tough guy.

148
00:09:25,280 --> 00:09:29,380
I activate this, my
scapegoat card. Oh, no!

149
00:09:35,160 --> 00:09:38,900
Sorry, but your attack
failed, rich boy! Awesome!

150
00:09:39,340 --> 00:09:41,477
Joey's scapegoat absorbed Kaiba's attack!

151
00:09:41,560 --> 00:09:45,060
And he's still got three
scapegoats left. Too bad.

152
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:49,777
My life points aren't going anywhere
as long as these guys are on the field.

153
00:09:49,860 --> 00:09:52,180
Well, they won't be for long.

154
00:09:52,760 --> 00:09:55,640
Blade Knight, destroy
his second scapegoat!

155
00:09:58,460 --> 00:10:02,000
Hey, why did your Blade Knight
just gain more attack points?

156
00:10:02,300 --> 00:10:05,377
Because Blade Knight has a
special ability, that's why.

157
00:10:05,460 --> 00:10:10,057
It gains 400 attack points when I
have one card or less in my hand.

158
00:10:10,140 --> 00:10:16,500
So now it has a strength of 2,300, and
my Blue Eyes has 3,000 attack points.

159
00:10:16,780 --> 00:10:20,880
And thanks to the devastating effect
of my all-powerful crush card,

160
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:24,280
you have no monsters with more than 1,500.

161
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:28,920
Kaiba may be an arrogant jerk,
but the guy does have a point.

162
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:31,680
It's your move now.

163
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:36,593
How can I take down two of Kaiba's
heavyweights with a deck full of wimps?

164
00:10:36,820 --> 00:10:38,100
You're going down.

165
00:10:38,560 --> 00:10:39,480
Look out!

166
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:44,757
Not exactly what I was hoping for, but I
guess it can help guard my life points.

167
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:47,016
First, I'll place one card face down.

168
00:10:47,800 --> 00:10:50,506
Then I'll play Battle
Warrior in defense mode.

169
00:10:50,700 --> 00:10:52,120
And that's all for now.

170
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:55,220
That pathetic monster won't slow me down.

171
00:10:55,500 --> 00:10:57,441
Well, we'll just see about death.

172
00:11:00,520 --> 00:11:05,400
So you left a piece of your
mind inside this girl. How sad.

173
00:11:06,300 --> 00:11:09,300
Yes, and it's my
responsibility to stop you.

174
00:11:10,140 --> 00:11:11,480
Is that so?

175
00:11:11,740 --> 00:11:15,400
Don't you realize that you
don't exist anymore, Marek?

176
00:11:15,540 --> 00:11:17,720
I occupy your body now.

177
00:11:18,860 --> 00:11:22,260
I know, and I've returned
to reclaim it from you.

178
00:11:22,520 --> 00:11:25,020
I'm afraid you're too weak now.

179
00:11:25,460 --> 00:11:31,160
Marek, I'm the real you, and you're
nothing but a small piece of my memory,

180
00:11:31,460 --> 00:11:32,700
thanks to Odeon.

181
00:11:33,540 --> 00:11:37,380
Because of his accident, I
was able to emerge again.

182
00:11:37,720 --> 00:11:39,220
Oh, Odeon.

183
00:11:41,880 --> 00:11:44,180
I told you you were too weak.

184
00:11:47,640 --> 00:11:48,760
Sorry, Marek,

185
00:11:48,920 --> 00:11:53,861
but it's time for me to banish what's left
of you into the shadows where you belong.

186
00:11:55,700 --> 00:11:58,840
I'm afraid there's nowhere
left for you to run now.

187
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:02,340
You won't get away with this.

188
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:05,737
You're in no position to make threats.

189
00:12:05,820 --> 00:12:08,020
I drove you out once.

190
00:12:08,180 --> 00:12:10,200
Now it's time to finish the job.

191
00:12:12,660 --> 00:12:13,954
That's what he thinks.

192
00:12:19,660 --> 00:12:23,160
You're just prolonging
your demise. Goodbye.

193
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:30,380
You're nothing without
Odeon to protect you.

194
00:12:30,740 --> 00:12:32,681
It's time to end our little game.

195
00:12:32,900 --> 00:12:35,660
You'll never meddle in my affairs again.

196
00:12:38,020 --> 00:12:39,440
It's over!

197
00:12:40,460 --> 00:12:41,680
It's over!

198
00:12:43,820 --> 00:12:45,200
Stop this at once! Huh?

199
00:12:45,520 --> 00:12:47,200
Stay out of this, Ishizu!

200
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:51,700
This doesn't concern you!

201
00:12:53,820 --> 00:12:55,960
Then again, I could banish you both!

202
00:12:56,580 --> 00:12:57,700
Be gone!

203
00:12:57,980 --> 00:13:00,100
You're not my brother! Sister!

204
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:02,340
It's too late! What?

205
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:05,037
I have grown weak, Ishizu!

206
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:07,880
Stop him, but forget me!

207
00:13:09,060 --> 00:13:10,480
Merrick, get up!

208
00:13:10,720 --> 00:13:12,640
I'm the only Merrick now!

209
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:15,320
I occupy his body, Ishizu!

210
00:13:15,700 --> 00:13:18,080
Now it's time for you to go!

211
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:22,420
Prepare to reunite with your
father in eternal darkness!

212
00:13:24,080 --> 00:13:28,000
I'm going to enjoy this
immensely! Hold on!

213
00:13:30,020 --> 00:13:31,520
Look at this!

214
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:33,520
I'm quite popular today!

215
00:13:35,540 --> 00:13:39,140
All right, this has gone
far enough, Merrick.

216
00:13:39,420 --> 00:13:40,840
Ah, welcome, Pharaoh.

217
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:43,828
Our battle will begin
sooner than I thought.

218
00:13:49,720 --> 00:13:51,779
Two great forces are now colliding.

219
00:13:56,880 --> 00:14:00,400
On second thought, I don't
want to end this just yet.

220
00:14:00,680 --> 00:14:03,200
That would be too easy, Pharaoh.

221
00:14:04,380 --> 00:14:06,977
and i have something more fun in mind

222
00:14:07,060 --> 00:14:11,817
so until then good day when we next

223
00:14:11,900 --> 00:14:18,337
meet your power will be mine look

224
00:14:18,420 --> 00:14:22,300
what's tea doing up here is she all right

225
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:26,917
tea has been through quite
a bit but she should be fine

226
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:30,353
soon but why would she have
come here in the first place.

227
00:14:30,520 --> 00:14:31,640
Poor girl.

228
00:14:32,340 --> 00:14:36,360
Pharaoh, my brother's good
side still lives. I know.

229
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:37,740
But there's more.

230
00:14:38,100 --> 00:14:40,380
He lives within Taya's mind.

231
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:44,220
But soon, he could be gone forever.

232
00:14:46,460 --> 00:14:49,900
You're no match for my
monsters and it's my move.

233
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:54,140
I play the magic card, card of demise.

234
00:14:54,820 --> 00:14:58,217
This card marks the beginning
of the end for you, Wheeler.

235
00:14:58,300 --> 00:14:59,180
Yeah?

236
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:00,737
And why's that, Kaiba?

237
00:15:00,820 --> 00:15:03,000
Because I draw five cards now.

238
00:15:03,300 --> 00:15:06,460
But in five turns, I lose my entire hand.

239
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:10,061
Of course, I plan to destroy
you long before that.

240
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:12,637
Just how are you gonna do that, Kaiba?

241
00:15:12,720 --> 00:15:15,320
Let me make my move and I'll show you how.

242
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:19,440
I summon Kaiser Seahorse in attack mode.

243
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:25,380
Kaiser Seahorse, attack
his scapegoat. Nah!

244
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:29,620
Now, Blade Knight, go!

245
00:15:33,900 --> 00:15:36,000
And now for my blue eyes!

246
00:15:36,220 --> 00:15:37,860
Destroy his battle warrior!

247
00:15:43,360 --> 00:15:44,320
Oh, man!

248
00:15:44,580 --> 00:15:46,997
Now Joey doesn't even
have one monster left!

249
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:50,797
And if he doesn't do something soon,
Kaiba will wipe out his life points.

250
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:52,200
That's enough for now.

251
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:56,017
So why don't you go ahead and try
to get yourself out of this mess?

252
00:15:56,100 --> 00:15:58,197
Unless, of course, you've
come to your senses.

253
00:15:58,280 --> 00:16:00,868
In which case, you'll
just give up, Wheeler.

254
00:16:02,020 --> 00:16:04,160
I guess you don't know me very well.

255
